{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting","id":1058607,"title":"Hoping to get some help on Lasting","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-05T15:28:09-08:00","id":1058607,"title":"Hoping to get some help on Lasting","content":"So, I know I may be opening a can of worms by inviting discussion of Lasting. But in the Reach to change Primary Factor thread, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> correctly identified that the issue I was having with that rule stemmed less from the rule itself and more from the book operating on guidelines that it did not thoroughly explain - &quot;whatever you think of as a more powerful version of the spell&quot; did not lead me to the correct assessments of what certain example spells' primary factors should be, and I blamed primary factors being locked to certain effects rather than the instructions being lacking. They also identified a set of guidelines that were extremely helpful for correctly assessing Primary Factors, which as pretty much resolved the issue for me.<br /> <br /> I was hoping we might be able to develop similar guidelines for what makes an effect Lasting. The book says only &quot;When a spell ends, look at what it changed, if anything, in the environment. Those are its Lasting qualities.&quot; which has similarly lead me to the wrong conclusions about whether part of an effect should be Lasting or not. Can we put our heads together and come up with a set of clear, objective rules for what makes part of a spell's effect naturally Lasting, and what qualifies a spell's effect for being able to be made Lasting with +2 Reach?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:35:27-08:00","id":1058612,"title":"","content":"&quot;Lasting&quot; is even more contentious and confusing than the Primary Spell Factor issue.<br /> <br /> I,too, would welcome additional clarity and guidance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:38:04-08:00","id":1058614,"title":"","content":"Lasting, in general, is a very important &quot;switch&quot; or &quot;lever&quot; for GM to manipulate. Deciding on what is Lasting or not in your game massively shapes the setting and can be used for making the game low magic, high magic, horror, power fantasy, and for manipulating many other qualities. While figuring out what could be &quot;Lasting or not&quot; by default rules, it's also very important - if not more important - to understand what your Mage game wants to be Lasting.<br /> For example, a lot of Life Magic seems to not be Lasting - especially spells that regenerate. This leads into a Mage Society where you can do a lot of miracles, but there are still cripples and overcoming your disability isn't just a case of finding a Life 4 Cleric in the town to cast Regeneration. Do you want this to be case in your game? <br /> Any ruling on Lasting will have...I'm sorry...lasting effects on your setting. Be careful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:40:12-08:00","id":1058615,"title":"","content":"Lasting usually seems to be the indirect result of a spell, for those instances when it's not it appears to be because it's taking advantage of the possibility of a thing to exist naturally despite the thing be forced by that spell in this particular instance. Souls belong in bodies, Hallows can theoretically exist anywhere, etc. There are some that seem to be exceptions to those general rules, Scribe Grimoire for instance, although theoretically you could have one delivered to you by a Supernal being you summon it which might makes its existence &quot;natural&quot; enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T15:58:32-08:00","id":1058623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058614#post1058614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lasting, in general, is a very important &amp;quot;switch&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;lever&amp;quot; for GM to manipulate. Deciding on what is Lasting or not in your game massively shapes the setting and can be used for making the game low magic, high magic, horror, power fantasy, and for manipulating many other qualities. While figuring out what could be &amp;quot;Lasting or not&amp;quot; by default rules, it's also very important - if not more important - to understand what your Mage game wants to be Lasting.<br /> For example, a lot of Life Magic seems to not be Lasting - especially spells that regenerate. This leads into a Mage Society where you can do a lot of miracles, but there are still cripples and overcoming your disability isn't just a case of finding a Life 4 Cleric in the town to cast Regeneration. Do you want this to be case in your game? <br /> Any ruling on Lasting will have...I'm sorry...lasting effects on your setting. Be careful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, Dave B of all people has specifically stated that Regeneration is non-Lasting. But totally agree with you on Lasting spells shaping the setting<br /> <br /> In fact, that might be the single most important factor here, despite how I too dislike arbitrary limits. More on this after some thought (and listening to what others have to say)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:03:48-08:00","id":1058626,"title":"","content":"Yeah, there was a...heated discussion...about this where people were really angry about the fact that you are one dispel away from losing your regenerated limb or heart or whatever. I was, instead, incredibly excited by the idea that a Mage trying to help their grandma will live in terror thinking what will happen if spell runs out or if people will use that Sleeper disbelief thing to dissolve it.<br /> As you probably can see, setting where this is a case is *vastly different in tone and colour* from one where you can literally go and save whole hospitals of grandmas forever as an Instant Spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:17:07-08:00","id":1058633,"title":"","content":"So I think we can at least agree that the natural side-effects of a spell are always Lasting - if you use Life to give someone a fatal heart attack, you don't have to spend 2 Reach to keep them from coming back to life because the actual effect of the spell was giving them the heart attack; death is simply a totally non-magical result of having suffered a heart attack. Are there any exceptions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:30:30-08:00","id":1058642,"title":"","content":"Oh, and we can add a rule that spells that regenerate limbs can never be made lasting. I'm not sure the in-world reason for that, but frankly that's not what I care about for the purposes of this discussion. Rather, I am interested in discerning by inductive reasoning the unwritten rules the writers were using to decide which abilities would get that +2 Reach option and which ones wouldn't. If &quot;regeneration spells don't ever get that option&quot; is one of those rules, it should go on our list. We can always house rule out rules we disagree with once we've established what they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-05-2017, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:37:16-08:00","id":1058647,"title":"","content":"In the case of regeneration, you are altering someone's shape. That is a direct result of the spell.<br /> <br /> The nonsequitor is that *all* healing should not be lasting. That is the exception to the rule","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:40:31-08:00","id":1058649,"title":"","content":"Hmm. It's less &quot;regenerate limbs&quot;, and more of &quot;spells that drastically modify the basic template of the subject&quot;, with the template not in mechanical sense but more of a &quot;natural shape&quot;. I'm not sure how to express it, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:44:53-08:00","id":1058651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058633#post1058633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I think we can at least agree that the natural side-effects of a spell are always Lasting - if you use Life to give someone a fatal heart attack, you don't have to spend 2 Reach to keep them from coming back to life because the actual effect of the spell was giving them the heart attack; death is simply a totally non-magical result of having suffered a heart attack. Are there any exceptions?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really good question. Apparently, using Life to speed a plant's growth is not Lasting (see Accelerate Growth). Would using Time to do the same follow the same ruling, or would the growth just be a natural result of a lot of time passing artificially quickly? I have no idea, though my intuition is that Time is probably(?) supposed to have the same problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:54:29-08:00","id":1058657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058649#post1058649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. It's less &quot;regenerate limbs&quot;, and more of &quot;spells that drastically modify the basic template of the subject&quot;, with the template not in mechanical sense but more of a &quot;natural shape&quot;. I'm not sure how to express it, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could it be said that Lasting generally applies to things that could conceivably (if not reasonably) happen naturally? Like, healing grievous wounds vs. regenerating limbs. You could, in theory, recover from a bullet wound to the head, but you couldn't regenerate a limb that got hacked off. Just on a cursory reading of the book, this <i>kind of </i>holds up...the exception being spells that have explicitly supernatural (Death, Spirit, etc.), which are bound to the CofD cosmology, so the given definition of &quot;naturally&quot; is fluid there.<br /> <br /> That being said, there are (many) things that can't be made Lasting that you can do naturally -- raising an Attribute or Skill, for instance. I guess the caveat is things that are bought with XPs can't be Lasting, which is more of a meta reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:56:37-08:00","id":1058659,"title":"","content":"I think the overriding idea is that the effects of magic are not Lasting, except when it wouldn't make sense otherwise (healing, damage, and similar effects), plus some explicit exceptions that are mostly about Matter spells being more permanent because of thematic reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:58:31-08:00","id":1058660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058659#post1058659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the overriding idea is that the effects of magic are not Lasting, except when it wouldn't make sense otherwise (healing, damage, and similar effects), plus some explicit exceptions that are mostly about Matter spells being more permanent because of thematic reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all healing. Don't forget about the regeneration exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:00:52-08:00","id":1058664,"title":"","content":"My interpretation of Accelerate Growth is that it makes biological matter behave as if it had grown older rather than actually becoming older. If the subject's cells actually did age like that the subject would most likely die due to the cells not being able to reproduce before dying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:05:35-08:00","id":1058670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fortunatus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058651#post1058651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a really good question. Apparently, using Life to speed a plant's growth is not Lasting (see Accelerate Growth). Would using Time to do the same follow the same ruling, or would the growth just be a natural result of a lot of time passing artificially quickly? I have no idea, though my intuition is that Time is probably(?) supposed to have the same problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... I was going to say that I think the effect of the spell is to make the subject grow faster for the Duration, and that its state after the Duration was a natural consequence of having a faster growth rate during that time. But then the spell says &quot;When the spell expires, the subject returns to its actual age.&quot; Weird. Though the fact that the spell's text specifies this makes it clear that it is an intentional exception to the general rule, and that without that clarifying statement the results of magically having your growth rate enhanced would normally be naturally Lasting. So we can probably tack &quot;unless otherwise specified by the spell&quot; onto the general rule and be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:06:26-08:00","id":1058671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058660#post1058660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all healing. Don't forget about the regeneration exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth noting that you can heal boxes of damage and still be missing fingers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:07:45-08:00","id":1058672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058660#post1058660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not all healing. Don't forget about the regeneration exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think of regeneration as healing, since for humans it's not natural. Although It is an interesting question what would happen if you give some one the ability to regenerate lost limbs like a lizard (like Dr. Connors from Spiderman) with Transform Life, and then dispel the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:12:30-08:00","id":1058674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058659#post1058659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the overriding idea is that the effects of magic are not Lasting, except when it wouldn't make sense otherwise (healing, damage, and similar effects), plus some explicit exceptions that are mostly about Matter spells being more permanent because of thematic reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is the case. There is at least a consistent theme of the mundane consequences of a spell being naturally Lasting - see my fatal heart attack example, or the book's example of the flames remaining after a spell to create fire ends. The effect of the spell was to create fire without a catalyst, the flames themselves are a natural result of flammable things in the area having been in contact with fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:14:30-08:00","id":1058675,"title":"","content":"As a side thought, it's worth noting that Regeneration ban doesn't really stop Thyrsuses from healing people from these things - instead of using Life to do that, you use Spirits of healing. Spirit is probably the fastest way to get reliable, undispellable way of ressurecting people (through Ressurection Numina).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:17:42-08:00","id":1058682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058657#post1058657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Could it be said that Lasting generally applies to things that could conceivably (if not reasonably) happen naturally? Like, healing grievous wounds vs. regenerating limbs. You could, in theory, recover from a bullet wound to the head, but you couldn't regenerate a limb that got hacked off. Just on a cursory reading of the book, this <i>kind of </i>holds up...the exception being spells that have explicitly supernatural (Death, Spirit, etc.), which are bound to the CofD cosmology, so the given definition of &quot;naturally&quot; is fluid there.</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly is fluid, given the text of Accelerate Growth, since living beings naturally grow. By the &quot;only if it's natural&quot; metric, would Regeneration then be Lasting if cast on a starfish?<br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, the reasoning is that Lasting is decided such that the RPG functions the way players generally expect an RPG to function (damage being generic health lost which can then be regenerated, while specific effects of damage like limb loss and blindness are subject to different rules, and so on). I hope I'm wrong on that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","user":"Fortunatus","date":".  I got the spell's name wrong. [i]sigh[/] 03-06-2017, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:19:34-08:00","id":1058683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058657#post1058657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could it be said that Lasting generally applies to things that could conceivably (if not reasonably) happen naturally? Like, healing grievous wounds vs. regenerating limbs. You could, in theory, recover from a bullet wound to the head, but you couldn't regenerate a limb that got hacked off. Just on a cursory reading of the book, this <i>kind of </i>holds up...the exception being spells that have explicitly supernatural (Death, Spirit, etc.), which are bound to the CofD cosmology, so the given definition of &amp;quot;naturally&amp;quot; is fluid there.</div> </div> </div> </div>If this is the case though, would regeneration spells be able to be made Lasting when cast on werewolves?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058657#post1058657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That being said, there are (many) things that can't be made Lasting that you can do naturally -- raising an Attribute or Skill, for instance. I guess the caveat is things that are bought with XPs can't be Lasting, which is more of a meta reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, a meta reason is more than enough for the purposes of this discussion. As I said, I'm more interested in figuring out <i>what</i> the rules are for now than <i>why</i> they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:22:13-08:00","id":1058685,"title":"","content":"It might be that the Regeneration spell isn't Lasting even on beings that can naturally regenerate because it's not designed to utilize the natural regenerative capabilities (it doesn't make a limb regenerate as much as it makes a limb just grow). Rather, the regular healing spells could probably be used to regenerate limbs on beings capable of regenerating limbs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":". 03-05-2017, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:24:11-08:00","id":1058688,"title":"","content":"Quick one before going to sleep, so take it with a grain of salt because I didn't check the spells:<br /> <br /> If the state that the spell directly imposes by itself could be represented by a Persistent Condition, or removing of one, the spell may not be lasting. <br /> <br /> If a *consequence of the spell* creates condition, it's ok. But if *the spell* would be the condition, it's not. Ugh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:24:25-08:00","id":1058689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058685#post1058685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be that the Regeneration spell isn't Lasting even on beings thqt can naturally regenerate because it's not designed to utilize the natural regenerative capabilities (it doesn't make a limb regenerate as much as it makes a limb just grow). Rather, the regular healing spells could probably be used to regenerate limbs on beings capable of regenerating limbs.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes a lot of sense, actually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:36:39-08:00","id":1058697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058674#post1058674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think this is the case. There is at least a consistent theme of the mundane consequences of a spell being naturally Lasting - see my fatal heart attack example, or the book's example of the flames remaining after a spell to create fire ends. The effect of the spell was to create fire without a catalyst, the flames themselves are a natural result of flammable things in the area having been in contact with fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>My list of examples was just that and not exhaustive, and your counter examples would all be &quot;similar effects&quot; in my view. They are things that wouldn't actually make sense for them to revert back once the spell end.<br /> <br /> I understand regenaration is a special grey area where to many people it would make more sense for it to be Lasting, but it's still debatable and is explicitly called out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:46:12-08:00","id":1058702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058697#post1058697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My list of examples was just that and not exhaustive, and your counter examples would all be &amp;quot;similar effects&amp;quot; in my view. They are things that wouldn't actually make sense for them to revert back once the spell end.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this explanation is that it doesn't resolve my issue of the guidelines for what is or is not Lasting being too subjective. If anything &quot;things that it wouldn't make sense to not be permanent&quot; is even more open to interpretation than &quot;things that have changed in the environment after the spell has ended&quot;, which is exactly what I don't want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T17:51:31-08:00","id":1058704,"title":"","content":"One spell that perplexes me most of all is Create Sympathy. It's Lasting by default (which already is unusual for a Making spell, but I can buy that) and the created Sympathy is still subject to fading just like naturally created Sympathy. But there's a Reach option that makes it permanent. I really don't get that. It's not how Sympathy works so why the hell would the spell be able to do that as a Lasting effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T18:00:27-08:00","id":1058713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058702#post1058702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with this explanation is that it doesn't resolve my issue of the guidelines for what is or is not Lasting being too subjective. If anything &quot;things that it wouldn't make sense to not be permanent&quot; is even more open to interpretation than &quot;things that have changed in the environment after the spell has ended&quot;, which is exactly what I don't want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spell effect are by default not Lasting EXCEPT 1) They are explicitly said to be 2) It would defeat the purpose of the spell (meaning that the spell would be completely useless and not merely inconvinient or resource intensive to use) if the effect would revert after Duration ends. Couple that with differentiating effect and consequences. The consequences of spells are all Lasting. What reverts back if the specific and explicit effect of a spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T18:07:07-08:00","id":1058715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058713#post1058713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spell effect are by default not Lasting EXCEPT 1) They are explicitly said to be 2) It would defeat the purpose of the spell (meaning that the spell would be completely useless and not merely inconvinient or resource intensive to use) if the effect would revert after Duration ends. Couple that with differentiating effect and consequences. The consequences of spells are all Lasting. What reverts back if the specific and explicit effect of a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>How would a healing spell be completely useless if it weren't Lasting? Heal in combat to survive, then keep healed until hospital or other care can be obtained. That's useful, though inconvenient.<br /> <br /> Edit: the point being that I don't think your criteria explain the healing-regeneration dichotomy well. Tessie seems closer to the point on that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","user":"Fortunatus","date":". 03-05-2017, 09:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T18:15:04-08:00","id":1058719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058713#post1058713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It would defeat the purpose of the spell (meaning that the spell would be completely useless and not merely inconvinient or resource intensive to use) if the effect would revert after Duration ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>This part is too subjective. Too much room for different people to come to different conclusions about whether or not a spell would be made useless (see Forunatus' response about healing spells, for instance). What I'm after is objective criteria, things that don't rely on the player's or ST's personal judgment to assess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T01:31:22-08:00","id":1058824,"title":"","content":"The only thing I've really allowed explicit application of reach to get Lasting for is the Shaping spell. It was for something like repairing a broken phone. In general I tend to allow it if it's something that could reasonably be a permanent effect without the use of magic. This excludes things like regeneration of limbs (in most cases). I certainly don't have an explicit list of what can made Lasting and what can't be, though. I just allow or disallow on a case-by-case basis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13082-projectmoon","name":"projectmoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T02:03:28-08:00","id":1058832,"title":"","content":"Mage is a difficult one for me to follow and Lasting is one of the reasons why but I'm trying to come up with some rules for Lasting. Pick apart as you will.<br /> <br /> 1. A spell with a description that states an effect is lasting at the base spell level or when using reach has an effect that is lasting as indicated.<br /> 2. A spell that has an effect that explicitly indicates a reversion to the state before the spell has an effect that is not lasting as indicated.<br /> 3. Rules 1 and 2 rule over all other rules.<br /> 4. A spell's direct effect is not lasting but side effects, secondary effects or effects resulting from the direct effect of a spell (depending on how you want to phrase it) are lasting.<br /> 5. A spell effect that could be viewed as a secondary effect but is literally just a restatement of a direct effect is not lasting.<br /> <br /> niche cases<br /> 6. Damage is lasting.<br /> 7. Reversing damage (healing) is lasting. (Regeneration does not reverse damage in a mechanical sense, no health boxes)<br /> 8. Healing poisoning is lasting, healing diseases is lasting as long as this could occur without magic.<br /> 9. Spells that grant knowledge do not provide lasting knowledge, but spells that grant a means to acquire knowledge do.<br /> <br /> I shall explain my thinking on the niche cases. It should be obvious for the general rules.<br /> <br /> Spells that deal damage actually don't inflict damage as a direct effect. For example, if a spell rots flesh and bone that is the direct effect and the side effect of flesh and bone rotting is recording damage. I assume the rotting fades away when the duration is over but the damage is already done at that point. Wacky, but that is magic for you.<br /> <br /> I view healing damage as reversing damage because that is the only way it really falls under rule 4 and not 5. This is not an arbitrary distinction. It is difficult to describe healing beyond the &quot;secondary effect&quot;. Healing magic speeds up natural healing processes so that is why it is lasting. As a more gritty option, healing need not be lasting, but I don't think that is how most people want it to go anymore than they want damage to go away when a duration ends.<br /> <br /> The spell that heals poison falls squarely under rule 4 to me based on the description. Diseases is less clear but I think it works the same way, but that requires the caveat that the disease must be curable, all poisoning is technically if not practically.<br /> <br /> A spell that grants a bonus to a skill or attribute should not be lasting but some sort of clairvoyance should allow you to learn information which is lasting.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the burning things, heart stopping, etc., I have some thoughts. I don't know of a spell that creates fire except Create Energy and that doesn't say the fire sticks around. I think of it like an old D&amp;D fireball. You throw the fireball and an area is engulfed in flames. Those flames don't last but anything in the area that would be burned by being engulfed in flames is burned and anything that would catch fire, catches fire. If this was a special fireball that lasts multiple rounds then that means more things burn or catch fire, but the flames from the fireball still extinguish at the end of the duration. If you create fire on a pile of firewood then the firewood will continue to burn because you set the firewood on fire. Contrast that with creating fire on glass.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure Death can stop a person's heart. Since it can stop muscles, I wouldn't say it is impossible. Speaking of that, Rule 5 on stopping muscles to create Tilts. I don't think the book covers instant kill spells, but I'm sure it is possible at some point, so let's say there is a spell that just flat out kills someone, sucks the life right out of them. This would have a secondary effect of stopping the heart and all brain activity. After a few minutes, it doesn't matter if the person &quot;comes back to life&quot; when the duration ends because the body is too far gone. First stage would be a vegetative coma. Second stage would be a body that no doctor could save because of natural decomposition processes. Now if the spell preserves the body after death then that is different.<br /> <br /> This brings me to all the different ways to do the same thing that means sometimes the effect would be lasting and sometimes not. Accelerated Growth is an example. Rule 2 means the growth isn't lasting but what if you use Time? If you use time to accelerate growth then that is the exact same spell and should work the same. However, if you created a pocket where Time moved faster within than without then I think growth should be lasting because that is not the direct effect of the spell. The direct effect of the spell is to create an area where everything within experiences time at a faster rate. I think the million ways to do a particular thing is what creates much confusion.<br /> <br /> I use those example to illustrate how the rules work. I'm not debating the nature of how the spells work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T03:20:35-08:00","id":1058857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058832#post1058832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think the book covers instant kill spells, but I'm sure it is possible at some point, so let's say there is a spell that just flat out kills someone, sucks the life right out of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are Unmaking spells that straight up annihilates something, and they should be Lasting. The watsonian answer would be something like when it no longer exists it's not dependent on the spell to stop existing. The doylist answer is that when it stops existing it would no longer be the target for the spell and start existing again immediately unless the effect is Lasting.<br /> This is in contrast to Making spells where most stuff that is created ex nihilo requires the spell to continue existing since their existence is a direct effect of the spell. (But Create Sympathy completely breaks that pattern for reasons unknown.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058832#post1058832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This brings me to all the different ways to do the same thing that means sometimes the effect would be lasting and sometimes not. Accelerated Growth is an example. Rule 2 means the growth isn't lasting but what if you use Time? If you use time to accelerate growth then that is the exact same spell and should work the same. However, if you created a pocket where Time moved faster within than without then I think growth should be lasting because that is not the direct effect of the spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely, but it would most likely have to be a higher Practice for Time to do something like that. I'm not terribly familiar with Time but it sounds like a four dot spell to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T07:41:20-08:00","id":1058985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1058832#post1058832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excellent post</div> </div> </div> </div>This is exactly the sort of thing I was looking for, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T08:20:05-08:00","id":1059006,"title":"","content":"In order to help me think about this, I put this list together. It might be useful for others, so I'm sharing it. Also, some comments about Diggs' rules below.<br /> <br /> Things that are explicitly noted as Lasting are:<br /> * healing spells (though it's ambiguous whether that includes spells that resolve Conditions, Tilts, and other effects that simulate injury beyond simple health boxes lost)<br /> * anything that would logically be changed in the environment after the spell's Duration ends<br /> <br /> Example spells that are explicitly noted as Lasting:<br /> Death<br /> * Soul Jar w/+2 Reach<br /> * Exorcism<br /> Fate<br /> Sever Oaths w/+2 Reach<br /> Matter<br /> * Integrity w/+2 Reach<br /> Mind<br /> * Clear Thoughts w/+2 Reach<br /> * Mind Wipe w/+2 Reach<br /> Prime<br /> * Dispel Magic w/+2 Reach &amp; 1 Mana<br /> * Scribe Grimoire w/+1 Reach &amp; 1 Mana<br /> * Hallow Dance w/+2 Reach &amp; 1 Mana<br /> * Supernal Dispellation w/+2 Reach &amp; 1 Mana<br /> * Blasphemy w/+2 Reach<br /> * Create Truth w/+2 Reach &amp; 5 Mana<br /> Space<br /> * Cut Threads<br /> * Create Sympathy w/+1 Reach<br /> Spirit<br /> * Banishment<br /> Time<br /> * Shifting Sands<br /> * Corridors of Time<br /> <br /> I didn't see anything that directly conflicts with Diggs' set of rules from the game mechanics end of things.<br /> <br /> I do have a quibble with Diggs' rule 8. I see no reason to treat poisons and diseases differently. In both cases, removing the source of the problem still leaves at least some damage done. And, there are plenty of poisons that are not technically curable; most heavy metal poisoning being an example.<br /> <br /> I also disagree with some of the rationales given, as they contradict the text of some of the spells in question. Life-Force Assault, for example, states, &quot;This involves rending that Pattern, causing horribly painful internal wounds and unspecific tissue damage.&quot; I don't think it's reasonable to read that as anything other than the spell directly damaging its target, rather than the damage being a side-effect of what the spell does. As with all things, though, mileage probably varies with the reader.<br /> <br /> That said, the rules Diggs presented are excellent, IMO. I'm still mulling them over, so I'm not sure if I'd amend them yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T09:40:04-08:00","id":1059042,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fortunatus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1059006#post1059006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order to help me think about this, I put this list together. It might be useful for others, so I'm sharing it. Also, some comments about Diggs' rules below.<br /> <br /> Things that are explicitly noted as Lasting are:<br /> * healing spells (though it's ambiguous whether that includes spells that resolve Conditions, Tilts, and other effects that simulate injury beyond simple health boxes lost)<br /> * anything that would logically be changed in the environment after the spell's Duration ends<br /> <br /> Example spells that are explicitly noted as Lasting:<br /> Death<br /> * Soul Jar w/+2 Reach<br /> * Exorcism<br /> Fate<br /> Sever Oaths w/+2 Reach<br /> Matter<br /> * Integrity w/+2 Reach<br /> Mind<br /> * Clear Thoughts w/+2 Reach<br /> * Mind Wipe w/+2 Reach<br /> Prime<br /> * Dispel Magic w/+2 Reach &amp; 1 Mana<br /> * Scribe Grimoire w/+1 Reach &amp; 1 Mana<br /> * Hallow Dance w/+2 Reach &amp; 1 Mana<br /> * Supernal Dispellation w/+2 Reach &amp; 1 Mana<br /> * Blasphemy w/+2 Reach<br /> * Create Truth w/+2 Reach &amp; 5 Mana<br /> Space<br /> * Cut Threads<br /> * Create Sympathy w/+1 Reach<br /> Spirit<br /> * Banishment<br /> Time<br /> * Shifting Sands<br /> * Corridors of Time</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! This is incredibly helpful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fortunatus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1059006#post1059006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't see anything that directly conflicts with Diggs' set of rules from the game mechanics end of things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, so it's probably pretty functional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fortunatus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1059006#post1059006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do have a quibble with Diggs' rule 8. I see no reason to treat poisons and diseases differently. In both cases, removing the source of the problem still leaves at least some damage done. And, there are plenty of poisons that are not technically curable; most heavy metal poisoning being an example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I would probably put poison and disease in the same category as Tilts and Conditions - not 100% sure yet if removing them is Lasting or not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fortunatus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1059006#post1059006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also disagree with some of the rationales given, as they contradict the text of some of the spells in question. Life-Force Assault, for example, states, &quot;This involves rending that Pattern, causing horribly painful internal wounds and unspecific tissue damage.&quot; I don't think it's reasonable to read that as anything other than the spell directly damaging its target, rather than the damage being a side-effect of what the spell does. As with all things, though, mileage probably varies with the reader.</div> </div> </div> </div>It makes sense to me. This may be a bit meta, but the way I see it, the internal wounds and tissue damage are the direct effects of the spell, and the /s, Xs, or *s marked in the victim's health boxes are a natural consequence of internal wounds and tissue damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T09:59:05-08:00","id":1059051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1059042#post1059042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you! This is incredibly helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>No problemo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1059042#post1059042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes sense to me. This may be a bit meta, but the way I see it, the internal wounds and tissue damage are the direct effects of the spell, and the /s, Xs, or *s marked in the victim's health boxes are a natural consequence of internal wounds and tissue damage.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Way</i> too meta for my blood. I see the the ticks in the boxes as a way for players to represent said wounds and damage, not as a &quot;natural consequence&quot; of those things. The character sheet simply doesn't exist in the game world, and it therefore has no place in any justification for the way things work from an in-game perspective. Until a character's fireball sets my dining room table on fire, I'm going to see any talk about the natural consequences of spells as coming from an in-game perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T10:13:18-08:00","id":1059057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fortunatus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1059051#post1059051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Way</i> too meta for my blood. I see the the ticks in the boxes as a way for players to represent said wounds and damage, not as a &amp;quot;natural consequence&amp;quot; of those things. The character sheet simply doesn't exist in the game world, and it therefore has no place in any justification for the way things work from an in-game perspective. Until a character's fireball sets my dining room table on fire, I'm going to see any talk about the natural consequences of spells as coming from an in-game perspective.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, like I said, it's a meta explanation and probably won't work for everyone. I kinda see it as like the heart attack example on a smaller scale, but I can see why its an unsatisfactory explanation for many.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T13:58:17-08:00","id":1059185,"title":"","content":"So far, separating what the spell actually does to create an effect from the effect itself seems to set a good metric.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T19:24:07-08:00","id":1059314,"title":"","content":"Cool. I guess I'm not completely lost.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11887_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11887\" data-vbnamecard=\"11887\">Tessie</a> exactly<br /> <br /> Diseases are complicated because sometimes a disease is the effect of another disease. Within the rules sometimes a disease would be represented as a condition rather than the norm. I think poison and disease (generally) should be treated the same so I made a rule to include both. Perhaps, different wording would be better. My intention is to exclude disease that doesn't work with disease rules.<br /> <br /> As I read the description of that cure poison spell, it seems to affect an organism by improving ability to eliminate poisons, bending rather than breaking the laws of reality. The side effect is, with enough successes, the poison can be eliminated. The spell to cure diseases seems to mechanically work the same without the description indicating how it works. If the rule has both work the same, as I think should be the case, then both cures would be lasting and damage done needs to be treated another way.<br /> <br /> I haven't gotten to creating spells so I'm not looking at Practices yet. I don't want Practices in my rules determining how Lasting works. I want a brief list I can run down as needed. Now if there is obvious higher magic that indicates it would more permanently cure poisons and diseases then I would go with that for Lasting effects, but then why include spells to temporarily treat? I can see value in halting the progress for a duration. Temporarily removing these problems so they come back at the end of the duration seems like a dumb spell to me. How is that better than freezing progress? I can see not having space to provide a halting spell but having a halt without a cure seems odd. Does not compute.<br /> <br /> Inflicting and healing damage is a paper thin line when it comes to whether it should be lasting or not. However, I think most people would respond to the notion that it would not be lasting with WTF even low magic can do that. There is definitely a meta element there. I would tend to think of it more precisely as the direct spell effect is whatever inflicts the damage and the side effect is the damage. There is a distinction because maybe the Mage misses or the target is immune. Thin, but I just can't see these effects not being lasting as the norm.<br /> <br /> Paralyzing a leg to create a leg tilt is the same as inflicting damage to tick a health box, restatement of effect or mechanical representation of the effect as you prefer. Creating an electric shock to paralyze a leg or inflict damage is one effect leading to another. Best explanation I can offer.<br /> <br /> I don't have all the spells memorized. Is there a spell that cures tilts or conditions? I can consider how it works with my rules if I have the spell description. I don't think the most direct way to inflict tilts, conditions, poison or disease would be lasting. The variety of methods allows for some to be lasting. Feature, not bug. Lasting within Life and Time was where I usually get confused so I tend to limit my view there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T02:54:29-08:00","id":1059410,"title":"","content":"I actually think that damage is lasting can be easily explained via the side effect rule. Inflincting damage isn't it itself something the spell does, since damage is not an additional state you inflict on somebody, it is the game's way of describing the fact, that part of a living beeing is destroyed. So what damaging spells actually do is using various ways of causing destruction, while the destruction itself is just the side effect. If I incenerate a house with a magical torch it has been established that it does not just miracoulsy stands there undamaged after my torch goes out.<br /> <br /> I have a lot more difficulty coming up with the same reasoning for healing spells though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T04:08:43-08:00","id":1059430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1059410#post1059410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually think that damage is lasting can be easily explained via the side effect rule. Inflincting damage isn't it itself something the spell does, since damage is not an additional state you inflict on somebody, it is the game's way of describing the fact, that part of a living beeing is destroyed. So what damaging spells actually do is using various ways of causing destruction, while the destruction itself is just the side effect. If I incenerate a house with a magical torch it has been established that it does not just miracoulsy stands there undamaged after my torch goes out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I go back to Life-Force Assault, whose description is the direct shredding of a living being's Pattern. That's not damage via a conjured medium. The same goes for Mind Flay. It seems like a heck of a stretch to me to say that either of those spells causes damage indirectly. <br /> <br /> Beyond that, the whole notion of separating cause from effect in these cases strikes me as specious hair-splitting at best. One might as well argue that gashing me with a knife is merely a way of causing destruction, and that any damage I take from that gash is just a side effect. That logic would make every spell Lasting. My character's spell didn't actually <i>do</i> anything, it just served as the <i>cause</i> of [insert effect here].","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T05:13:41-08:00","id":1059445,"title":"","content":"Your second paragraph is actually exactly my reasoning. Damaging spells are basically magical knifes (whatever weapons) the mage gashes someone with. I think the same is true for Life-Force Assault, you are rending the pattern of a subject with magic, so the magic acts as a weapon. I don't see how it would follow that every spell is lasting from this. If I use Mind to implement false memories into a subject, the memory as well as the process of connecting the memory to the brain of the subject are made out of magic and when that magic dissolves, so does the false memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T07:35:59-08:00","id":1059497,"title":"","content":"The issue with Life-Force Assault and Mind Flay exists only because of a lacking spell description. Mind Flay does mumbo jumbo so damage is inflicted. LF Assault isn't really better. This isn't about how the spell does what it does, which can be a problem for every spell, but what the spell does. I'm talking about what the spell does in the story, not game mechanics. So, this happens with some spells, they have black-box effects.<br /> <br /> I have a choice. I can say the spell works differently than almost all that do something similar for some reason or all damage dealing spells create or manipulate forces and objects to inflict damage just like every damage dealing spell that I can actually explain. I choose that the spells work the same even when I don't know how.<br /> <br /> None of that actually matters. It is acceptable to simply state damage is lasting as a rule. My preference is to tie logically niche case rules to the broader rules which are based on examples and explanations within the book. It isn't required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T16:02:55-08:00","id":1059804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1059445#post1059445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your second paragraph is actually exactly my reasoning. Damaging spells are basically magical knifes (whatever weapons) the mage gashes someone with. I think the same is true for Life-Force Assault, you are rending the pattern of a subject with magic, so the magic acts as a weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not the way I see it, though, in retrospect, I could have used a better example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1059445#post1059445\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how it would follow that every spell is lasting from this. If I use Mind to implement false memories into a subject, the memory as well as the process of connecting the memory to the brain of the subject are made out of magic and when that magic dissolves, so does the false memory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, my version of that spell does not implant a false memory. Instead, it warps the mind of a subject, so the magic acts as a tool that sculpts false memories into being. Hence, a Lasting false memory springs into being simply because I opted for semantics that seemingly put my spell at a remove from its intended effect. That's the way I see the whole &quot;Life-Force Assault is just a magic weapon&quot; notion, and that's why I call it specious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T16:11:17-08:00","id":1059806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1059497#post1059497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of that actually matters. It is acceptable to simply state damage is lasting as a rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed in full.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1059497#post1059497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My preference is to tie logically niche case rules to the broader rules which are based on examples and explanations within the book. It isn't required.</div> </div> </div> </div>My preference would be to simply have the rules, and let magic be capricious and mysterious in-game. I don't really see a need for magic to be more consistent than is necessary to tell interesting stories, so long as a robust set of rules keeps game-play fair (consistency being one of the cornerstones of fairness).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","user":"Fortunatus","date":". 03-07-2017, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","name":"Fortunatus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12791_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T16:38:47-08:00","id":1059826,"title":"","content":"Life Force Assault messes with bodily functions enough to cause varied forms of tissue damage. It may simultaneously briefly stop air or blood flow, make muscles pull each other apart until they tear, make your kindneys and liver stop working or make your blood preasure so high your arteries burst. When all those eefects end and your body resumes normal functioning, you find it's pretty wrecked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12673-ew-matias","name":"EW-Matias","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"245"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T18:40:17-08:00","id":1059865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EW-Matias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1058607-hoping-to-get-some-help-on-lasting?p=1059826#post1059826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life Force Assault messes with bodily functions enough to cause varied forms of tissue damage. It may simultaneously briefly stop air or blood flow, make muscles pull each other apart until they tear, make your kindneys and liver stop working or make your blood preasure so high your arteries burst. When all those eefects end and your body resumes normal functioning, you find it's pretty wrecked.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and I interpret rending a Pattern differently. C'est la vie.<br /> <br /> Let's get back to making a list of objective rules that work well, rather than attempting to justify those rules with game metaphysics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12791,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12791-fortunatus","user":"